}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"xy8kh6553","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Let the dough rise in a loaf pan that has been sprayed with oil, covered loosely with plastic wrap for about 30 minutes to 1 hour while preheating your oven to 375 degrees.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"9pco86555","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"662j06557","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"After the dough has risen 1/2 to 1 inch or so above the rim of your loaf pan, remove the plastic wrap and put it on the middle rack in the preheated oven for 35-40 minutes. It will rise even more in the oven so be sure it's not too close to the top element. Turn the loaf front to back halfway through to ensure even baking and color. When it's done it will sound quite hollow on top when tapped.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"j788n6559","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"6uc6g6561","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Brush it with melted butter and let it cool for about 10 minutes before loosening it from the pan. Let cool at least 45 minutes before slicing.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-02-17T23:10:48.613Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-02-17T23:10:48.613Z","id":"faa2b616-421c-41b3-803f-48c5985190b8"},"documentStyle":{}},"instructions":"Mix all of the dry ingredients then add the butter and sourdough starter.\n\n​\n\nSlowly add a cup of the warm milk while the mixer is running on low speed until the dough begins to come together adding more if you need it a tablespoon at a time. You can add a bit more flour if you go over and it gets too sticky. Let the mixer knead the dough 6-7 minutes more.\n\n \n\nNow scrape the dough out of the mixer and onto a floured board. Knead the dough by folding it over on itself and turning it 4 times then shape it into a ball. Roll it around in a large bowl with a little good quality oil to coat it then cover it with plastic wrap to rise for about 1 1/2 hours.\n\n \n\nAfter the dough has risen to approximately double in size you can form your loaf by folding it over on itself once or twice then rolling the dough up like a newspaper and pinching closed the seem. Check out my tutorial for Soft Sprouted Wheat Multigrain Sourdough Sandwich Bread to learn more about rising and forming the loaf.\n\n \n\nLet the dough rise in a loaf pan that has been sprayed with oil, covered loosely with plastic wrap for about 30 minutes to 1 hour while preheating your oven to 375 degrees.\n\n \n\nAfter the dough has risen 1/2 to 1 inch or so above the rim of your loaf pan, remove the plastic wrap and put it on the middle rack in the preheated oven for 35-40 minutes. It will rise even more in the oven so be sure it's not too close to the top element. Turn the loaf front to back halfway through to ensure even baking and color. When it's done it will sound quite hollow on top when tapped.\n\n \n\nBrush it with melted butter and let it cool for about 10 minutes before loosening it from the pan. Let cool at least 45 minutes before slicing.","title":"Sourdough Sandwich Bread with ground flax and almonds"},{"introduction":"Chocolate Rye Sourdough Bread is so pretty! It has only a slight chocolate flavor so it's really a savory bread. The rye is enhanced by the chocolate and you taste a both sweet and savory explosion of flavor not unlike a good stout beer.","servings":"10-12","photo":"image://v1/577c92_2b4431f99d1b4f448fd4633ea9a4b82e~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/4032_3024/20180425_150053.jpg","link-recipes-1-title":"/bread-and-sourdough/chocolate-rye-sourdough-bread","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/chocolate-rye-sourdough-bread","image":"wix:image://v1/577c92_2b4431f99d1b4f448fd4633ea9a4b82e~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/20180425_150053.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","_id":"c403886c-9455-47b2-b276-12a08d7dc117","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-02-17T18:37:31.227Z"},"title1":"Chocolate Rye Sourdough Bread","shortDescription":"Chocolate Rye Sourdough Bread is so pretty! It has only a slight chocolate flavor so it's really a savory bread. The rye is enhanced by the chocolate and you taste a both sweet and savory explosion of flavor not unlike a good stout beer.","link-recipes-1-all":"/recipes-1/","cookingTime":"40 minutes","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-02-18T21:53:00.060Z"},"recipesCatagoryCatagory":"/Recipes/catagory/Bread","preparationTime":"3 hours","ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"2 1/2 cups All Purpose Flour","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"9yai76823","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"1/2 cup rye flour","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle"